> level of the character.  I'm asking, because if I had realized the
> potential danger of carrying a cockatrice, I'd probably have put it in my
> bag.

Other sudden-death situations that come to mind (and how to prevent
them):
























- choking over your food; don't eat when satiated, and avoid eating
large monsters unless you're really hungry (tin large
intrinsic-granting monsters)

- deadly poison; get poison resistance as soon as you can (lot of
non-poisonous monsters have it)

- gazing upon the Medusa; have a blindfold/towel handy (mirror helps
too)

- being drowned by an eel; I genocide the buggers, otherwise just stay
away or charm them or something.  Don't try hacking at them if there's
more than one (and you're not wearing an amulet of magical breathing)
or you're asking for it.  I've heard levitating helps too, which makes
sense but I haven't tried it.

- being squished by a drawbridge; I always just destroy the drawbridge
with a wand of striking and levitate over it, otherwise stay well
clear.

- wand o'death, finger o'death; have reflection, or a really low armor
class.  

- being decapitated by a monster wielding Vorpal Blade (well, it COULD
happen :) )

